From: Abbas Rizvi <abbas.rizvi@nomadrail.com>
Subject: [TRIAG-8585 #11] Puppet — TFTP conntrack helper on the CCU firewall

Repo:  Puppet / deployment
Env:   dostoneu_migration_mar5
Where: the `60-allow-management` firewall fragment (exact module path varies by
       your Puppet layout — this is the iptables/raw rule + module load it needs)

Problem
-------
`obn update f ap` batch firmware pushes silently fail for most APs. The CCU
firewall has no TFTP conntrack helper, so the data-channel (random high UDP
port) of the RFC1350 TFTP transfer is not associated with the udp/69 control
flow and gets dropped by default-DROP. Only ~5 of 15 APs succeed, by
conntrack-race luck. Field workaround today (runtime-only, lost on reboot):

    modprobe nf_conntrack_tftp
    iptables -t raw -I PREROUTING -p udp --dport 69 -j CT --helper tftp

This must become permanent in the CCU image via Puppet.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Reference implementation (adapt to your Puppet firewall module idiom)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

1) Ensure the kernel module is loaded at boot:

   # /etc/modules-load.d/nf_conntrack_tftp.conf  (manage via Puppet file{} )
   nf_conntrack_tftp

   -- or, if you use the `kmod` module --
   kmod::load { 'nf_conntrack_tftp': }

2) Add the CT helper rule to the raw/PREROUTING chain in 60-allow-management.

   If the fragment is templated iptables-restore, add to the *raw table*:

       *raw
       -A PREROUTING -p udp --dport 69 -j CT --helper tftp
       COMMIT

   If you use the puppetlabs-firewall module:

       firewall { '060 tftp conntrack helper':
         chain  => 'PREROUTING',
         table  => 'raw',
         proto  => 'udp',
         dport  => 69,
         jump   => 'CT',
         helper => 'tftp',
       }

Acceptance for #11
------------------
On a fresh CCU pulled from Puppet, with no hand-patching:
  lsmod | grep nf_conntrack_tftp        # module present
  iptables -t raw -S PREROUTING | grep 'dport 69 .* CT --helper tftp'   # rule present
Then `obn update f ap` (batch) completes for all APs, not ~5/15.
